n class=\"strong\">Are</span> you <span class=\"strong\">planning</span> to change the format to save space on the disk?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Which files are</span>  you <span class=\"strong\">converting</span> tomorrow?</span><br/><br/> Remember, you use the present continuous tense in its interrogative form to ask about a plan when it is already arranged."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, and after explaining this concept, are you giving any example in context?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you planning to give a lecture about data conversion?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, is the user converting files immediately? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Countable and Uncountable Nouns with Some and a Piece Of"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">countable and uncountable nouns</span> to talk about quantities of different elements that you can or can't count."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this opportunity, we are going to focus on two important quantifiers: <span class=\"strong\">some </span> and <span class=\"strong\">a piece of</span>. Take a look at the following chart to learn some aspects about them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are a lot of different pieces of data that usually vary from application to application or change over time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Every word processing program includes some special codes for features."}, {"type": "example", "content": "After conversion when there is no equivalence in codes, the system doesn't display some features the same as they appear in the original file. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's a good piece of advice, I need to discuss that issue in the lecture."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">QUANTIFIERS</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Some</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can use the quantifier <span class=\\\"strong\\\">some</span> with both countable and uncountable nouns.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples:<br/></br>   <ul> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Some</span>  information</br><li> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Some</span> markets</span></br> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Some</span> software programs </span></span></li></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">A Piece of</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can use the quantifier <span class=\\\"strong\\\">a piece of</span> with uncountable nouns.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples:<br/></br>   <ul> <li><span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">A piece of</span> data</span></br><li> <span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">A piece of</span> information</span><br/></br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conversion "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something is transformed into a different element"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can say that data conversion is the process of transforming and transferring data from one format to another."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "upgraded"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that is enhanced or improved "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some markets include data conversion facilities to read files from their competitors' products or from upgraded versions. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "incompatibility"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that is not compatible, considered as discordant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  He normally finds incompatibility in programs from different vendors or between an earlier and a late version."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feature "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a characteristic or a peculiarity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The system doesn't display some features the same as they appear in the original file."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Nisus Writer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an Apple Macintosh program for word processing, specially used by book authors"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Imagine that a user who has Nisus Writer sends a file to a user with Microsoft Word, he will certainly have a compatibility issue."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "indent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a space that indicates margins"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Every word processing program includes some special codes for features, such as indents and pagination."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le02ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about compatibility between Microsoft and Mac."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write your findings about compatibility between Microsoft and Mac on your notebook."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read about conversion data tools for these kind of software. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your findings with your teacher and your classmates."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about compatibility between software."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about compatibility between software."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read about conversion data utilities. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about compatibility with my classmates and my teacher."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Common Collocations in Computer Science"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">collocations</span> to talk about computer science topics in case you need to mention the steps of a process or to provide any specific instruction. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some common <span class=\"strong\">collocations</span> are the following:<br/><br/><ul><li>maintain a web page.<li>Re-install a program.<li>Delete a file.<li>Use predictive text.<li>Record a video.<li>Transform data.<li>Make it readable.<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Data conversion is the process of transforming and transferring data from one format to another."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Data conversion works in order to make a piece of information readable in a different software or application."}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": "", "_data": [], "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Carol:</strong> Are you planning to give a lecture about data conversion?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Steven:</span> Yes. So far I can say data conversion is the process of transforming and transferring data from one format to another because there are a lot of different pieces of data that usually vary from application to application or have changed over time.<br/>\n<strong>Carol:</strong> Well, I know you are explaining that concept; are you giving any example in context?<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "28000", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Steven:</strong> Yes. When a user deals with a word processing program, he normally finds incompatibility in programs from different vendors or between an earlier and a late version. For example, if a user who has Nisus Writer sends a file to a user with Microsoft Word, he will certainly have a compatibility issue, even if the receiver has a later Nisus version; the conversion may be needed.<br/>\n<strong>Carol:</strong> OK. So, is the user converting files immediately? Or what is he supposed to do?<br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob01re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "64500", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Steven:</strong> Yes. Data conversion works in order to make a piece of information readable in a different software or application.  Thus, every word processing program includes some special codes for features, such as indents and pagination; that might not be the same in other formats.<br/>\n<strong>Carol:</strong> Well, nowadays it is not a major issue because some markets include data conversion facilities to read files from their competitors' products or from upgraded versions. The real problem is that after conversion when there is no equivalence in codes, some features are not displayed as in the original file, which is a good piece of advice you need to discuss in the lecture. <br/>", "image": "enpe7n3le02ob01re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n3le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le02ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": "", "questi